1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,914
Welcome to the QuickBooks to Odoo nineteen migration wizard.

2
00:00:03,914 --> 00:00:07,829
Here we're setting up the connection.

3
00:00:07,829 --> 00:00:11,744
You can choose QuickBooks Online, using OAuth, where we request permission to read your GL, AR, and AP.

4
00:00:11,744 --> 00:00:15,659
Or QuickBooks Desktop, where you upload a QBX export file.

5
00:00:15,659 --> 00:00:19,574
The wizard walks you through authentication or file selection, then validates that we can read your data.

6
00:00:23,696 --> 00:00:27,763
Next, we configure how your QuickBooks accounts map to Odoo.

7
00:00:27,763 --> 00:00:31,829
The wizard shows your QB account list and proposes mappings to Odoo GL accounts.

8
00:00:31,829 --> 00:00:35,895
You can review, override, and save these mappings.

9
00:00:35,895 --> 00:00:39,962
Mappings are versioned, so if you run the migration twice with different mappings, both runs are recorded separately.

10
00:00:46,186 --> 00:00:49,759
Here we've extracted your QuickBooks GL.

11
00:00:49,759 --> 00:00:53,333
The wizard shows a preview:

12
00:00:53,333 --> 00:00:56,906
transaction count, date range, GL account coverage, and any validation warnings.

13
00:00:56,906 --> 00:01:00,480
If you see issues, like missing accounts or unexpected balances, you can adjust mappings and re-extract.

14
00:01:00,480 --> 00:01:04,053
Once you approve, the data is loaded into staging.

15
00:01:07,967 --> 00:01:11,547
Before going live, the finance controller reviews reconciliation.

16
00:01:11,547 --> 00:01:15,128
We show your QB trial balance and the Odoo trial balance side by side.

17
00:01:15,128 --> 00:01:18,708
We highlight variances:

18
00:01:18,708 --> 00:01:22,289
missing accounts, rounding differences, or mapping errors.

19
00:01:22,289 --> 00:01:25,869
You sign off on each variance, and the reconciliation report is locked with your approval date and signature.

20
00:01:28,401 --> 00:01:32,423
Once reconciliation is approved, you can go live.

21
00:01:32,423 --> 00:01:36,444
All staged GL entries post to live Odoo accounts.

22
00:01:36,444 --> 00:01:40,466
The migration run is archived, and all staging tables are marked immutable.

23
00:01:40,466 --> 00:01:44,488
If you need to audit or prove what happened during migration, the archive is your evidence.

24
00:01:44,488 --> 00:01:48,509
The run log shows the extract timestamp, record counts, and who executed the migration.
